    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1026">

                <pb facs="0862" n="852" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg852"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.5493/12–149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bacon</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-01T16:00:00+08:00">December 1, 1949—4
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:40 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2520. Embtel 2482, November 26.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d1026-f1"/> Bacon and
                    Clough attended hearing re Labor Union after receiving phone call from Aliens
                    Affairs Office stating Union desired appearance Soule and Bacon. Soule’s absence
                    not commented on nor name mentioned at hearing. Employees’ demand for separation
                    allowance reduced to 2 months but maintenance and other demands renewed plus
                    demand that all payments based on wage scale be recalculated according to rise
                    cost of living. At conclusion Union official stated case transferred to Labor
                    Bureau which would begin preliminary investigation possibly December 3.</p>
                <p>Inform Peiping.</p>
                <p>Pass Army.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bacon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
